# Server Configuration
PORT=5000
FLASK_SECRET_KEY=change-this-secret-key-in-production

# Data Directory (optional - defaults to data/ or %LOCALAPPDATA%\MartPOS\)
# MARTPOS_DATA_DIR=/path/to/data

# Google Drive Backup (optional)
# Place credentials.json (OAuth "Desktop app" client) in the data directory,
# then use Settings -> Connect Google Drive. No env vars needed.

# Cloud messaging (optional) - the local POS only ever talks to the MartPOS
# gateway; Meta credentials live on the gateway, never here. This is
# deployment/build-operator configuration - not shop owner input. Packaged
# builds bake it via `npm run build:platform-config`; server-mode deployments
# may set it at runtime instead.
# MARTPOS_CLOUD_URL=https://gateway.example.com

# Required for storing cloud credentials (device token etc.) outside the
# Electron desktop app: base64-encoded 32-byte AES key. Under Electron, DPAPI
# is used instead and this is not needed.
# MARTPOS_SECRET_KEY=

# AI Store Manager (optional) - Google Gemini via Google Sign-In
# Customers connect a Google account in Settings -> AI Store Manager; they
# never see or enter an API key. The Gemini credential is backend-only:
#   MODE 1 (platform-managed): GEMINI_API_KEY set on the backend/host.
#   MODE 2 (managed):          POST /api/ai/config {api_key} stores it in the
#                              encrypted secrets store (internal/admin only).
#   MODE 3 (cloud-managed):    no local setup - cloud-linked installs pull
#                              the key from the MartPOS gateway
#                              (GET /v1/ai/credential) using their device
#                              token. Rotate the key on the gateway and
#                              installs re-fetch it automatically.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Model override (default gemini-3.8-flash); can also be set in Settings.
# GEMINI_MODEL=
# Google Sign-In needs an OAuth "Desktop app" client: place credentials.json
# in the data folder (same file Google Drive backup uses), set these, or let
# a cloud-linked install pull the client config from the gateway:
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
